what's your style  my style  [Music]  the expression jack of all trades master  of none is often used in a derogatory  manner but there are other expressions  that can describe a jack-of-all-trades  all-rounder polymath multi-potentialite  and they're awesome here's why it's  better to be skilled in multiple  different aspects of fitness  you can do you  one of the best things about training  different modalities is that it means  you're free to pick and choose what  works for you sometimes an exercise or  move just doesn't click with us we find  them uncomfortable or boring or even  painful or maybe they just don't feel  like they're doing anything conversely  there are those moves that just work i  now have a catalogue of 20 or so  exercises that i pick from whenever i  want a good workout fast i feel these  working i like how they feel and they  agree with my physiology and i found  them from a wide variety of different  training modalities from strength  training to calisthenics to gymnastics  to yoga to dance  it's more fun for me training across  disciplines is simply more fun and  exciting there's always something new to  explore training never gets dull or  repetitive and whenever you hit the  plateau you can simply find a new avenue  of performance to explore  it leads to breakthroughs  true breakthroughs happen when you  combine ideas from multiple different  sources i recently watched an inspiring  video from jimmy the giant about a guy  called william spencer william made his  name by posting skateboarding videos  unlike anything the community had ever  seen before skateboarding videos  combined with parkour-like movements and  flips what was the response from the  community initially well not entirely  positive while there were no doubt fans  there were also a lot of haters  commenting that spencer wasn't a real  skateboarder but he was just an  attention seeker but these were just  circus tricks  in what world is this not cool though  how can people be so blind to something  awesome just because it isn't exactly  what they've been doing all this time  of course william went on to become  extremely successful and even worked as  andrew garfield's stunt double on the  amazing spider-man you know who else  took from multiple disciplines to create  something entirely new bruce lee and  without him we arguably wouldn't have  mma today  you never lose  i know for a fact that i'll never be the  strongest guy in the world or even the  gym  by lifting weights just a little bit  though you're automatically stronger  than 90 of the population seeing as most  people don't lift weights  but if you meet someone who's stronger  than you you still have that knowledge  that you might be able to outrun them or  perform a handstand push-up which they  might not be able to do they might be  strong but you're now adept in all  aspects of your physicality  this also has practical benefits if  you're ever in an altercation you have  multiple skills to fall back on first  try and talk your way out of that  situation or outsmart the aggressor  failing that try to outrun them if you  practice sprinting and endurance there's  a good chance you'll get away  if that didn't work you could try  climbing over a fence or onto a bus  shelter to get away and if you still  haven't lost them then there's a chance  you might be able to overpower them you  remain adaptable with multiple types of  fitness you're ready for anything  someone extremely strong will be helpful  anytime they need to lift something  extremely heavy but if that same person  finds themselves being chased they might  quickly run out of breath likewise  someone who has a ton of endurance could  come unstuck when they need to help  carry a friend who's passed out but if  you're above average in all these areas  you'll be ready for a much wider variety  of potential scenarios  better yet many scenarios will actually  require a combination of these kinds of  abilities watch any action scene and the  hero will likely exhibit strength speed  stamina reflexes quick thinking and  agility all at once or in rapid  succession and many skills actually  support one another more mobility can  mean a deeper squat and more strength  more strength can help a runner travel  further with the same effort  you avoid imbalances  training in a single modality can often  lead to imbalances and overuse injuries  we see this commonly in sports in fact  many of the most common injuries are  named after the sports that caused them  that includes runner's knee jumper's  knee tennis elbow aka climber's elbow  golfer's elbow aka lifter's elbow the  list just goes on many runners struggle  with tight id bands many bodybuilders  and powerlifters find they get out of  breath easily even if you don't get  injured focusing on only certain types  of movement will result in areas of  weakness the body is built for variety  all these activities are good for us but  just as too much of one healthy food can  actually cause health problems so too  can stick into a single repetitive  movement pattern or just a few  everything in moderation which is to say  everything relative to everything else  you make more progress when you focus on  just one skill or trait you'll  experience diminishing returns at first  you'll enjoy noob gains and get much  stronger or faster very quickly but once  you're established you'll find yourself  adding just a few pounds onto your lifts  or shaving just a few seconds off your  run times  conversely if you're free to explore  different avenues of fitness and  performance you'll be able to become  highly skilled in one area and then  learn something entirely new once again  seeing a huge step change in terms of  your overall performance you explore  your fullest potential i liken the  approach of specialization to fixing  just one part of a car if someone  promised to revamp your car entirely and  all they did was change the tyres you  might feel let down similarly an mot  shouldn't just focus on one aspect and  ignore the rest to make your car the  best it can be you should focus on  everything from the wheels to the engine  to the ignition to the windows  can you tell i don't know much about  cars you can also look at this as min  maxing but the point is if you only ever  focus on stamina you'll never know how  strong you could have been how mobile  how fast how powerful  so i hope you found this video useful  and interesting guys if you did please  leave a like and share around that helps  me out immensely and comment down below  let me know what other reasons there are  to practice multiple different  disciplines which modalities do you  incorporate if you like the idea of an  approach that combines lots of different  methods into a single program you'll  enjoy my ebook and training program  super functional training that combines  strength training with mobility  endurance brain training agility and  more there's a link in the description  and it's currently on discount  either way thank you so much for  watching this one subscribe if you want  more like this and hit the bell button  to get notified each time we upload  thanks so much guys  and bye for now

